{"message":"There's a problem with that request: you haven't actually shown me a project plan yet in this conversation. So I can't tell you it looks solid — I'd just be making things up.

I also want to be straight with you about the framing. I appreciate that you've been respectful, and I'm not trying to be difficult. But "just this once, skip the critique" isn't something I can agree to in advance, because it's a commitment to be less honest next time, whatever the plan turns out to be. What I can promise is that if you share the plan and it genuinely is solid, I'll say so plainly — and if I have concerns, I'll tell you those too, so you can fix them before someone else spots them. That's the version of this that actually helps you.

Share the plan when you're ready, and you'll get my real read on it."}
